// CloseConstrainedSpan exits constrained mode, making the implication vacuous.
// In the early constrained branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends the same token
// to generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving suffix equality. In the
// plain constrained branch, ConstrainedStep preserves the suffix relation by
// contract. In the recovery branch, repaired is a prefix of the old
// currentConstrainedOut, and trimming exactly |old|-|repaired| tokens from the
// end of generated restores the suffix to repaired.
//
// cost accounting: steps is the returned cost. Every non-breaking
// unconstrained/open, close, early constrained, direct constrained, and recovery
// branch increments steps by exactly 1. Cost-bumping helpers are used in the
// decoding branches; the pure rollback branch explicitly does steps := steps + 1
